        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Reject future-dated attention requests",
        "body": "Closes #3\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes the attention request freshness check so future-dated `createdAt` timestamps cannot bypass stale request filtering.\r\n\r\n`AttentionRequest.consume()` now rejects timestamps whose distance from `now` is greater than `maxAge` in either direction. This preserves existing behavior for recent and undated requests while rejecting stale past requests and stale future requests.\r\n\r\nAdds a focused regression test for future-dated attention requests.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `swift build`\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n\r\n\r\nDirect proof against the built `NameplateCore` module:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF old-minus-600s returned=false fileExists=false\r\nPROOF future-plus-600s returned=false fileExists=false\r\nPROOF recent-minus-60s returned=true fileExists=false\r\nPROOF undated returned=true fileExists=false\r\n```",
